# UI usability

Contract: [`docs/examples/ui/usability.md`](../../docs/examples/ui/usability.md). Related maps: nested popups, tooltips, focus layers, dialog layout, persisted UI — see [`docs/examples/README.md`](../../docs/examples/README.md).

**Agent behavior:** if a change or existing panel violates the map, **warn and suggest** a concrete fix — do not refuse the work or invent large refactors unless asked. When touching a list/panel, briefly audit neighbors on the same surface.

Audience: casual automation beginners first. Prefer existing `theme::*` / `widgets::*` / `pickers::*` / `tip_*` helpers; extend opts instead of raw egui where a helper applies.

## Checklist (new or touched UI)

- [ ] Relevant Example Map opened/updated; every new green cites a test
- [ ] List/combo: sorted; filter or searchable combo if the set can grow
- [ ] Empty / no-match states have plain copy
- [ ] Local ↑↓ / Enter / Esc (or documented why not) without breaking record modes
- [ ] Icon-first labels with `h::` / `ht::` tip text where a glyph fits
- [ ] Beginner path visible; advanced options collapsed by default
- [ ] Reused shared tokens/widgets; layout matches a sibling of the same kind
- [ ] Icon/custom widgets AccessKit-labeled; stable ids in loops

## Out of scope unless asked

- New **global** application hotkey schemes
- Brand / theme redesigns
